Implement user story SKY-004a: Implement Express REST API server with /health, /search, /cheapest, and static dashboard endpoints

## Story Description
Create src/server.ts — an Express HTTP server exposing GET /health, GET /search, GET /cheapest, and GET / (static dashboard). Server reads PORT from env (default 3000) and RAPIDAPI_KEY from env. If RAPIDAPI_KEY is absent, /search and /cheapest return 503; /health and / are never gated. The listen() call is guarded so importing `app` in tests does not bind a port. The / route reads src/public/index.html at runtime via fs. Build script copies static assets to dist/public/. Add 'start' script in package.json pointing to 'node dist/server.js'. Depends on SKY-002.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Given the server module is imported without calling listen, Then no port is bound (the server does not start listening on import alone)
- Given the server is running, When GET /health is requested, Then the response is HTTP 200 with JSON body { status: 'ok', uptime: <number> } and Content-Type application/json; this route is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY absence
- Given the server is running, When GET / is requested, Then the response is HTTP 200 with HTML content read at runtime from src/public/index.html and Content-Type text/html; the HTML contains a search form and client-side JavaScript; this route is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY absence
- Given RAPIDAPI_KEY is set, When GET /search is called with valid from, to, date (and optional adults), Then the response is HTTP 200 { flights: FlightResult[], count, searchedAt (ISO-8601) }; adults defaults to 1 if omitted; empty results return { flights: [], count: 0 }
- Given RAPIDAPI_KEY is set, When GET /search is called with missing from/to/date, invalid date format, or adults≤0, Then the response is HTTP 400 with a JSON error body
- Given RAPIDAPI_KEY is set, When GET /cheapest is called with valid params and flights exist, Then the response is HTTP 200 with the cheapest FlightResult; missing params → 400; no flights → 404 { error: string }
- Given RAPIDAPI_KEY is absent, Then GET /search and GET /cheapest return 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; given the external API errors, they return 500 with a JSON error body; /health and / remain unaffected
- PORT env var is respected (default 3000); npm run build copies src/public/ to dist/public/ so the / route resolves correctly in both dev and built modes; start script runs node dist/server.js





